From e1aaec81cfad1267d96e686c66e6d3e9f48dbcbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:37:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] proc: report the emulated Seccomp: and TracerPid: in
 /proc/<pid>/status

A real kernel's /proc/<pid>/status describes that process: Seccomp: is its own
seccomp mode (0 disabled / 1 strict / 2 filter, fs/proc/array.c task_state) and
TracerPid: is the pid of its own ptracer, 0 when it is not traced.

FEX had no /proc/self/status creator, so opens fell through to the host file: the
guest read FEX's own seccomp mode and tracer, not its own.

Add a creator that rewrites only those two lines. Seccomp: comes from
ThreadStateObject::SeccompMode; TracerPid: is passed through unchanged when the
emulated process really is traced by an in-guest tracer (PtraceEmu::IsAttached)
and is 0 otherwise, which is what an untraced process reports. Every other line
is the host file's, unchanged - nothing else is fabricated. A host tracer that
exists only outside the emulated world is not an emulated-process fact, so it is
not exposed to the guest.

Base: FEX-2610 14c92681 + patches 0001-0010.
